From 1db4aad3b623a1703306db1c43c50edb255ad349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:41:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(methane): nitrogen closure and burial for the wetland
 tile (C-20)

Ledger C-20 (paper V2), four switches, all off by default. The wetland
tile gets its litter N from the prescribed plant input at C:N 46 with no
plant uptake, deposition, loss or vertical movement, so mineral N piles
up at depth (68-2,589 gN m-2 after spin-up) while the surface, where the
litter lands, holds almost none and litter-to-SOM immobilization is held
at fpi 0.04-0.2 at productive towers.

wetland_n_unlimited: immobilization runs at its potential rate and the
shortfall enters as supplemental N, as in CLM's carbon-only mode
(suplnitro = 'ALL'); fpi keeps the share the soil supplied.
wetland_n_uptake: the litter N is taken up from the mineral N left after
immobilization, in proportion to each layer's residual; fpg reports the
share the soil supplied.
wetland_vert_transp and wetland_burial_velocity: CLM's SOM mixing
(SoilBiogeochemLittVertTransp, bioturbation) on the wetland tile with a
downward advection for peat accretion, 12 g C m-2 yr-1 over 25 kg C m-3
(Wania et al. 2009 after Clymo 1984), about 4.8e-4 m yr-1.

The supplemental and uptake fluxes are cleared in the competition routine
only when their switch is on and used only under that switch, since the
wetland path never runs CNZeroFluxes.

